{title: When I Survey the Wondrous Cross}
{artist: Isaac Watts / Lowell Mason}
{genre: Easter}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{key_original: F}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}
{score: when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When I [G]survey the [C]wondrous [G]cross
On [Em]which the [D]Prince of [G]glory died
My [G]richest [C]gain I [G]count but loss
And [Em]pour con[D]tempt on [G]all my pride
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
For[G]bid it, [C]Lord, that [G]I should boast
Save [Em]in the [D]death of [G]Christ my God
All the [G]vain things that [C]charm me [G]most
I [Em]sacri[D]fice them [G]to His blood
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
See, [G]from His [C]head, His [G]hands, His feet
Sor[Em]row and [D]love flow [G]mingling down
Did e'er such [G]love and [C]sorrow [G]meet
Or [Em]thorns com[D]pose so [G]rich a crown
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Were the [G]whole realm of [C]nature [G]mine
That [Em]were a [D]present [G]far too small
Love so a[G]mazing, [C]so di[G]vine
De[Em]mands my [D]soul, my [G]life, my all
{end_of_verse}
